According to [[Casterwill family]] legend, Sorcerel came to Earth with her twin Titan, [[Sabriel]]. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}}

In the 17th century, Sorcerel was used by the Casterwill Seer, Michel de Notre Dame, better known as [[Nostradamus]]. Due to the close bond between Sorcerel and her Seeker, she became a Powerbonded Titan. {{Source|The Power of Kronos}} When [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] were sent back in time to the 17th century by the Legendary Titan of Time, [[Kronos]], they were attacked by [[Viktor Casterwill]] and Michel, who invoked Powerbonded Sorcerel. After fighting against [[Baselaird|Powerbonded Baselaird]], the two Titans defeated one another. {{Source|The Power of Kronos}}

Sorcerel's Amulet was eventually laid to rest in the [[Crystal Caves]]. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}}

Sophie was tasked with obtaining Sorcerel's [[Amulet]] from the [[Crystal Caves]] by [[Nimue Casterwill]] as a test of her allegiance to the Casterwill family. After being worn down by Nimue's [[Undine]] and [[Coralgolem]] Titans, Sophie was succeeded in passing the test thanks to the return of Sorcerel's sister, [[Sabriel]], now in Powerbonded form. Sophie was then able to invoke Sorcerel who swiftly defeated Coralgolem. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}}

Sophie invoked Sorcerel in the [[Casterwill Library]] in France to fight against [[Lucas|Lucas Casterwill's]] team. After defeating Lucas's [[Feyone]], Sorcerel was defeated by [[Lane|Lane's]] [[Wildwood Druid]]. {{source|Chasing Void}} On the Erasmus Bridge in [[Rotterdam]], Sophie called on Sorcerel to fight two [[Harlekin]] Titans summoned by [[Tantras|Tantras's]] orphan recruits. {{source|Den vs Harrison}} Sophie used Sorcerel to assist [[Baselaird|Powerbonded Baselaird]] against [[Freelancer]], [[Ironsquire]], and [[Hoplite]] Titans that had been possessed by [[Arc]], the [[Legendary Titan]] of Fate. After Lok used the Willblade to destroy Ironsquire's shield, Sorcerel was able to defeat it with a magical blast before being called back to her Amulet. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}

Sophie invoked Sorcerel to fight alongside Lok's [[Ironsquire]] against magical fear creatures whilst on a test to find [[Mythras]], the Legendary Titan of Valor. Due to being outnumbered, Sorcerel was defeated. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}

When [[Sophie Casterwill]] was fighting against [[Kiel]], she [[Powerbonded]] with Sorcerel, thus regaining her strength to fight Kiel. The newly empowered Sorcerel fought off the attacks of Kiel and his Titans, [[Vulcana]], and [[Balenpyre]]. After defeating Vulcana, Sorcerel was defeated defending Sophie from Kiel's [[Enderflame]] power. {{source|The Spiral War}}

Powerbonded Sorcerel was invoked by Sophie in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]] to fight against [[Harrison Fears|Harrison Fears']] significantly strengthened [[Antedeluvian|Powerbonded Antedeluvian]]. After forming the Triple Truth Shield with Powerbonded Sabriel, this was hindered when Sabriel was sent back to her Amulet by Harrison's [[Drybite]] power. After Dante's [[Ignatius]] defeated Antedeluvian, Sorcerel was called back to her Amulet. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

Sorcerel powerbonded with Sophie during her final battle with [[Kiel]]. Her appearance changed subtly, gaining a golden trim on her robe and a decorative golden headdress. She gained stronger magical blasts and force fields, and some new abilities:

*'''Honorforce''' - creates a reflective magical barrier to return attacks back to the enemy. This ability is proven strong enough to return three high-powered attacks from [[Kiel]], [[Vulcana]] and [[Balenpyre]] all at once. {{source|The Spiral War}} 

When used together with Sabriel and Sophie, they can activate the '''Triple Truth Shield''', a defensive barrier that protects all three of them and knocks back enemy forces. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

